the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 11. Contract [1], for 39,850 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of contracts with one awardee do not prove improper actions. These could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for patterns and review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same needs. Contract [1] could indicate a trend in late-year spending.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["N65dxnkQU1Z%2BF6L2uCfUWg%3D%3D","xlPOfTHhaPeTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","kElMqemrpYGIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}